en] > summary::before { transform:rotate(180deg); background-color:var(--c-tint); }\n.fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__item[open] > summary { color:var(--c-violet-600) !important; }\n.fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__h3 { margin:0; font-size:inherit; font-weight:inherit; line-height:inherit; color:inherit; flex:1; }\n.fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer { padding:0 22px 22px 64px; color:var(--c-fg-2); font-size:15.5px; line-height:1.7; }\n.fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer p { margin:0 0 10px; }\n.fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer p:last-child { margin-bottom:0; }\n.fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer a { color:var(--c-violet-600) !important; text-decoration:none !important; }\n.fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer a:hover { text-decoration:underline !important; }\n@media (max-width:760px) { .fmstr-cmp-apt-faq { padding:64px 16px; } .fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__item > summary { padding:16px; font-size:15.5px; gap:12px; } .fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer { padding:0 16px 18px 16px; font-size:15px; } }\n\u003C/style>\n\n<section class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq-h2">\n<div class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__container">\n<header class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__header"><h2 class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__h2" id="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq-h2">Common questions</h2></header>\n<div class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__list">\n\n<details class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__item">\n<summary><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__h3">Should I use this or just send a Calendly link?</h3></summary>\n<div class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer"><p>Use a Calendly link if all you need is the slot. Use an appointment form if you also need intake data, qualifying questions, file uploads, payment, or a custom confirmation email. The form layers everything around the slot in one step.</p></div>\n</details>\n\n<details class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__item">\n<summary><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__h3">Do I need a Calendly account?</h3></summary>\n<div class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer"><p>No. The Scheduler field can show fixed time slots you define directly in Formester. Connect Calendly if you already use it for team calendar management and want availability synced automatically.</p></div>\n</details>\n\n<details class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__item">\n<summary><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__h3">Can the booking only confirm after payment clears?</h3></summary>\n<div class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer"><p>Yes. Add Stripe or PayPal to the form. The slot books and the confirmation email fires only when the charge succeeds. Useful for deposit-required services, paid consultations, premium coaching.</p></div>\n</details>\n\n<details class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__item">\n<summary><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__h3">What does the booker see in their confirmation email?</h3></summary>\n<div class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer"><p>By default, a clean confirmation with the slot details. Edit the autoresponder to use any form field: "Hi {{first-name}}, your {{service-type}} on {{slot-date}} is confirmed. {{custom-instructions}}." Variables pull from the actual submission.</p></div>\n</details>\n\n<details class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__item">\n<summary><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__h3">Can the form handle different appointment types?</h3></summary>\n<div class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer"><p>Yes. Add a "What kind of appointment?" question at the top with conditional logic. Each answer can show a different scheduler with different available slots, different intake questions, and a different price.</p></div>\n</details>\n\n<details class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__item">\n<summary><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__h3">What time zones does the scheduler support?</h3></summary>\n<div class="fmstr-cmp-apt-faq__answer"><p>The scheduler shows the booker\'s local time automatically. Detect the time zone from the browser, or ask the booker explicitly at the top of the form for a more controlled experience (recommended for high-stakes bookings).</p></div>\n</details>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>'

